✅ What is API Versioning?
API versioning is the practice of managing multiple versions of an API so that changes to the API do not break existing clients.

It allows you to:

Introduce new features

Fix bugs

Modify response structures
...without affecting users depending on older versions.

✅ Common API Versioning Methods

| Method                  | Example URL / Usage                        | Notes                                          |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |
| **URI Versioning**      | `GET /api/v1/users`                        | Most common, easy to manage                    |
| **Header Versioning**   | `Accept: application/vnd.myapi.v2+json`    | Clean URLs, flexible, but harder to test/debug |
| **Query Param**         | `GET /api/users?version=2`                 | Easy but less RESTful                          |
| **Content Negotiation** | Based on `Accept` or `Content-Type` header | Advanced but rarely used fully                 |

