✅ How would you handle API responses that return different data types dynamically for the same field?

we have to use jsonnode methods to validate the response dynamically. For example, if a field can return either a string or an integer, you can use `JsonNode` methods to check the type before processing it.
| Approach                     | Description                                                                                   |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Use `JsonNode`               | Parse the response into a `JsonNode` object to handle dynamic types.                          |
| Check type with `isTextual()` | Use `node.isTextual()` for strings and `node.isInt()` for integers to determine the type.   |
| Use `asText()` or `asInt()`   | Convert the node to the appropriate type based on the check.                                  |
| Example                      | ```java<br>JsonNode node = response.jsonPath().get("field");<br>if (node.isTextual()) {<br>    String value = node.asText();<br>} else if (node.isInt()) {<br>    int value = node.asInt();<br>}<br>``` |
| Use `instanceof`             | If using Java objects, check the type with `instanceof` before casting.                        |


